var:LBANMETH a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBANMETH" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Record Qualifier, Perm, codelist LBANMET (C160922, Laboratory Analytical Method Calculation Formula); COSMoS does not use LBANMETH. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Analysis method applied to obtain a summarized result. Analysis method describes the method of secondary processing applied to a complex observation result (e.g., a calculation used to measure eGFR).' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBANMETH is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. SDTM CT puts the eGFR formulas (CKD-EPI, MDRD, Cockcroft-Gault) in LBANMET, not in the test code (the counter-case in Folded_Facets, Codelist_Phrases). No source says whether the calculation method is part of the observable. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: observable — a calculation method is a facet (docs/Observables_Direction.md); whether it changes the observable stays open." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LBBDAGNT a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBBDAGNT" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:Component ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "sources agree" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Variable Qualifier, Perm, no codelist in the IG table; COSMoS does not use LBBDAGNT (147 LB DSSs). SDTM v2.0: Variable Qualifier of --TESTCD (usage: CP, IS, and LB domains only). SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'The textual description of the agent that is binding to the entity in the LBTEST variable. The LBBDAGNT variable is used to indicate that there is a binding relationship between the entities in the LBTEST and LBBDAGNT variables, regardless of direction. LBBDAGNT is not a method qualifier. It should only be used when the actual interest of the measurement is the binding interaction between the 2 entities in LBTEST and LBBDAGNT. In other words, the combination of LBTEST and LBBDAGNT should describe the thing, the entity, or the analyte being measured, without the need for additional variables. The binding agent may be (but is not limited to) a test article, a portion of the test article, a related compound, or an endogenous molecule.' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBBDAGNT is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. The IG and Model notes say LBTEST with LBBDAGNT describes the analyte; one source states it, none contradicts. The same reading as ISBDAGNT, where COSMoS agrees. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8, LBBDAGNT-Notes. Kind: observable — follows from the position." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LBCOLSRT a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBCOLSRT" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:OpenFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Record Qualifier, Perm, codelist COLSTYP (C177908); COSMoS does not use LBCOLSRT (147 LB DSSs). SDTM v2.0: Variable Qualifier of --TESTCD; the SDTMIG v3.4 role (Record Qualifier) differs from the Model. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Used to indicate the type of collected summary result. This includes source summary results collected on a CRF or provided by an external vendor (e.g., central lab). If the summary result is derived by the sponsor using individual source data records from SDTM, the derived summary result is represented in ADaM. If the summary result is produced and reported by the lab, the collected summary result is represented in SDTM.' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBCOLSRT is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. No source says whether this variable is part of the observable. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: open — the Model ties the summary type to the test (observable); summarising several results is analysis, which is not a facet (docs/Observables_Direction.md)." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LBLLOD a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBLLOD" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:OpenFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Variable Qualifier, Perm, no codelist in the IG table; COSMoS does not use LBLLOD (147 LB DSSs). SDTM v2.0: Variable Qualifier of --TESTCD. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'The lowest threshold (as originally received or collected) for reliably detecting the presence or absence of substance measured by a specific test. The value for the field will be as described in documentation from the instrument or lab vendor.' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBLLOD is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. No source says whether this variable is part of the observable. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: open — a detection limit may separate tests (observable), or only describe the assay used, as received from the vendor (record)." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LBPDUR a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBPDUR" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:OpenFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Timing, Perm, no codelist in the IG table; COSMoS does not use LBPDUR (147 LB DSSs). SDTM v2.0: Timing (usage: Only in Findings class specimen-based domains: BS, CP, GF, IS, LB, MB, MS, MI, PC, PP). SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Planned duration of specimen collection. If LBPTFL is \"Y\" then LBPDUR is null.' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBPDUR is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. No source says whether this variable is part of the observable. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: open — as LBPTFL: how the specimen is collected (practice), or the time aspect of the observable (observable)." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LBPTFL a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBPTFL" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:OpenFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Timing, Perm, codelist NY (C66742); COSMoS does not use LBPTFL (147 LB DSSs). SDTM v2.0: Timing (usage: Only in Findings class specimen-based domains: BS, CP, GF, IS, LB, MB, MS, MI, PC, PP). SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'An indication that the specimen was collected at a single point in time. The value is \"Y\" or null. The intent of this variable in the LB domain is to aid mapping to LOINC codes in the dataset, when LOINC part \"Time Aspect\" = \"Pt\".' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBPTFL is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. No source says whether this variable is part of the observable. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: open — how the specimen is collected (practice), or the time aspect, a part of the LOINC code the IG note names (observable)." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LBRESSCL a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBRESSCL" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:Scale ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "sources disagree, decided by a stated rule" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Record Qualifier, Perm, codelist RSLSCLRS (C177910); COSMoS does not use LBRESSCL (147 LB DSSs). SDTM v2.0: Record Qualifier. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Classifies the scale of the original result value; for example, whether the result is ordinal, nominal, quantitative, or narrative.' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBRESSCL is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. COSMoS publishes result scale per BC, not as a DSS variable (Scale_Units in Domain_Behaviour). Rule (decided 2026-10-06, the scale row of this sheet): result scale is treated as distinguishing an observable, on the standards' own grounds; LBRESSCL is the LB variable that carries it. Basis as the scale row. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8, LBRESSCL-Notes. Kind: observable — follows from the position." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LBRESTYP a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBRESTYP" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Record Qualifier, Perm, codelist RESTYPRS (C179588); COSMoS does not use LBRESTYP (147 LB DSSs). SDTM v2.0: Record Qualifier. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Classifies the kind of result (i.e., property type) originally reported for the test. Examples include substance concentration, proportion, mass rate, and arbitrary concentration.' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBRESTYP is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. No source says whether the property type is part of the observable; the key has no property part. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: observable — the kind of quantity determined (a property, in LOINC's terms); whether it changes the observable stays open." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LBTESTCD a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBTESTCD" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:Component ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "sources disagree, decided by a stated rule" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "COSMoS puts GLUC and GLUCPE under one BC (C105585). SDTM CT publishes them as separate LBTESTCD terms with their own NCIt codes and definitions (GLUC C105585; GLUCPE C163446, \"plasma equivalent glucose\"). The key separates them; the fan-out does not. Rule (adopted 2026-10-08): a separate SDTM CT test term with its own NCIt code is a separate component (identity keyed on NCIt codes, Observables_Direction step 2). SDTM v2.0 and SDTMIG v3.4: Topic. Kind: observable — follows from the position." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "accepted" .

var:LBTPT a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBTPT" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:PracticeFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Timing, Perm, no codelist in the IG table; COSMoS does not use LBTPT (147 LB DSSs). SDTM v2.0: Timing; NCIt concept of --TPT: Study Data Tabulation Planned Time Point Name. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Text description of time when specimen should be taken. This may be represented as an elapsed time relative to a fixed reference point, such as time of last dose. See LBTPTNUM and LBTPTREF. Examples: \"Start\", \"5 min post\".' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBTPT is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. No source says whether this variable is part of the observable. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: practice — the planned time of the observation, set by the study design (as EGTPT)." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LBTSTCND a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBTSTCND" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Variable Qualifier, Perm, codelist TESTCOND (C181175); COSMoS does not use LBTSTCND (147 LB DSSs). SDTM v2.0: Variable Qualifier of --TESTCD (usage: CP, IS, and LB domains only). SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Identifies any planned condition imposed by the assay system on the specimen at the time the test is performed.' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBTSTCND is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. No source says whether this variable is part of the observable. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8, LBTSTCND-Notes. Kind: observable — a condition the assay imposes on the specimen, qualifying the test as --METHOD does; not a condition on the subject (unlike --FAST, --POS). Whether it changes the observable stays open." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LBTSTOPO a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBTSTOPO" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:OpenFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Domain_Variables in SDTM_Variables: SDTMIG v3.4 Variable Qualifier, Perm, codelist TSTOPOBJ (C181170); COSMoS does not use LBTSTOPO (147 LB DSSs). SDTM v2.0: Variable Qualifier of --TESTCD. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Text description of the high-level purpose of the test at the operational level.' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBTSTOPO is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. Two readings, as for ISTSTOPO (COSMoS value list in IS): the tier is part of the observable, or it is the operational step that produces it. No source says which. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8, LBTSTOPO-Notes. Kind: open — as the position: part of the observable, or the step that produces it (practice)." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

