ncit:C105585 skos:altLabel "GLUC",
        "Glucose" ;
    skos:definition "The determination of the amount of glucose present in a sample." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Glucose Measurement" ;
    cfa:umlsCui "C0337438" .

var:LBCAT a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBCAT" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:RecordFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "COSMoS: predicate GROUPS, \"groups values in\"; DEC not stated. No codelist; values without NCIt code. LBCAT and LOINC class are different groupings (LBCAT_LOINC_Class in Domain_Behaviour). No source says whether category changes the observation. SDTM v2.0 and SDTMIG v3.4: Grouping Qualifier. Kind: record — groups the records; carried, not keyed." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "accepted" .

var:LBFAST a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBFAST" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:PracticeFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "COSMoS: LBFAST is a value list (N;Y), never assigned, so it never separates sibling DSSs and is not in Variable_Evidence. LOINC (Subject_State in COSMoS_Observable_LOINC_Check): fasting-free and fasting-qualified glucose codes side by side (component Glucose^post CFst, class CHAL). LOINC offers fasting as a refinement, not as a requirement; no source says whether fasting is part of the observable. SDTM v2.0 and SDTMIG v3.4: Record Qualifier, like --SPEC and --METHOD; no published role separates subject state from identifying qualifiers. SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBFAST is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. COSMoS, LOINC and the IG agree that subject state is an optional refinement; none says it is always or never part of the observable (decided 2026-10-08: open, the conditional reading carried into Phase 2). Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: practice — fasting is a condition on the subject, set by how the observation is brought about (COSMoS and LOINC: subject state)." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "accepted" .

var:LBSPEC a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBSPEC" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:System ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:positionBasis "sources agree" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "COSMoS: predicate IS_SPECIMEN_TESTED_IN, \"is the specimen tested in\", codelist SPECTYPE. Fan-out axis specimen and key part system agree (Key_Compare in Domain_Behaviour). LOINC system agrees (LOINC_Compare in Domain_Behaviour); the exceptions are COSMoS pin errors reported by COSMoS_Observable_LOINC_Check. SDTM v2.0 and SDTMIG v3.4: Record Qualifier, the same role as --POS and --FAST; the role does not separate them. SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: with LBTEST and LBORRESU, 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code'. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: observable — follows from the position." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "accepted" .

